# ODAMP Security Model

## Threat Model

| Threat | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Single device compromise | FROST 2-of-3: one share is insufficient |
| Key share file theft | AES-256-GCM encryption, Argon2id KDF, 0600 permissions |
| Quantum adversary (key exchange) | ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203) during DKG |
| Sanctioned counterparty | OFAC SDN pre-flight screening, hard block |
| API compromise | JWT auth, rate limiting, read-only default |
| LLM prompt injection | Structured output, no execution authority, full logging |
| Supply chain | `cargo audit` in CI, lock files, pinned dependencies |

Key Lifecycle
DKG: Trusted dealer generates 3 shares. ML-KEM-768 for share exchange. Shares encrypted with AES-256-GCM (password → Argon2id → key).
Signing: 2-of-3 shares decrypt → FROST rounds → aggregate → Schnorr sig. Full key never exists.
Rotation: Re-run DKG. New Safe contract. Old shares deleted.

Audit Trail
All operations logged to PostgreSQL:

signing_logs: every FROST ceremony
compliance_logs: every screen (append-only)
ai_agent_logs: every LLM call (prompt hash, response, latency)
execution_logs: every trade (quote, fill, tx hash)
No log entries are ever deleted. Exportable for external audit.

